#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197976 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "81b0b6e1-41c3-5329-806e-162b8b27b045" :question/math-academy-id "e-12466" :question/problem "The lamina $D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\le x \\le y  ,\\, 0 \\le y \\le 1 \\big\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y) = x^2y.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nM_y = \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\lambda(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda(x,y) = x^2y .$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot {x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{\\int }_{0}^{y}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{y}^{5}}{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{6}}{24}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197977 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "9294903c-1b4c-58b6-a878-7f2220ec763d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12470" :question/problem "A thin plate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/3cfabe3c702883ca24c3188908c4cefeee43adb30797308828edd98374b5b44f.png) with the mass density function ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/ac38ea36432f3e278a4c2deb9203fbd5e486e348976e79157a5c6885a576f656.png) is enclosed between the curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/65b9fa371f35bfa31a21b50bc02f64561e4c838d71ebd99bf2d2d1c1be196dff.png) and the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/1fd42a46221d9624ec3d81db0f5c73cd8428ee2f8d80b5d7e4ff67e7018fb194.png)-axis  for ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/11d74a99b97245c1998471b33f9b9d0974e251345f825c475db4079c02fa273a.png) Find the moment of the plate about the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/b63bded3ee2ad150f576fd05c209caf32bd34853f4a7132fe4ee85b59b06f61a.png)-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/05ff793b0aee1f05a79216f9e7f119afa544749c81077937f8f06a353f6ef4eb.png) with the mass density function ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/bb3bf01e45585dbd5fe7732a1befa050d734bc46a466fea7f61f42851cfd3af8.png) about the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/d7d15efdd7573bd5b95e49ef05727ed1b8163a06781c393c1d3f27109fdc4eda.png)-axis is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/73a6e88adb05252ff114153227c13ae4f4adad9b676524179a20d9ae3d045d43.png)\n\nIn our case, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/33d4430552670d83a2c303e8ab286d3391f5611450f4e4f0b6ad6ccb58049b0e.png) is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/067543543031a1d8cb4ceb9a7901ad7db77629243adc6658d4a9eab3e98fe09f.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/03ccfab8b682725e94126f9fe59597d6e2886d3aeff64746681d0bbbed072520.png)\n\nand ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/17c342255c9bffbade441c02123bab3f7154e97b1a6a69a2874935f2dd684806.png) \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/ca38251cdd0a97967e8e6f4200e94b00571c5cfe2b84fef1991022e4fb976e62.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198165 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/id #uuid "8199670b-efe4-537b-8f8a-228d567a0944" :question/math-academy-id "e-8182" :question/problem "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y) = x+y$ and is enclosed between the curve $y=x$ and the $x$-axis for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ units and its center of mass is located at $( \\overline{x}, \\overline{y} ),$ what is the value of $\\overline{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overline{x},\\overline{y}) = \\left( \\dfrac{M_y}{m}, \\dfrac{M_x}{m} \\right),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\iint \\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_x = \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_y = \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/b872242423692a20a9d50658c99d9e8cee7c9b2737fb96592bc2bc35b4f72c32.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\:0 \\le x \\le 1, \\: 0 \\le y \\le x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda(x,y) = x+y.$ \n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot (x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}xy+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}xy+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}(\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{M_x}{m} = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{5}{24}\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)} = \\dfrac{5}{12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198166 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/id #uuid "37d7f2ae-90b0-5e6f-83c2-7cb21ed4f089" :question/math-academy-id "e-8183" :question/problem "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{1-y^2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-1 \\leq y \\leq 1.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area $A_D$ is given by $(x_c, y_c),$ where\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle x_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A, \\qquad \n\\displaystyle y_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/a7992c54f85f85cab3d9f923b8daca62c410393b364d30bcfbf5cff5efc93bbd.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\le x \\le \\sqrt{1-y^2}, \\: -1 \\le y \\le 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nA_D = \\dfrac12 \\cdot \\pi\\cdot 1^2 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}1-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{[y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(1-\\frac{1}{3})-(-1+\\frac{1}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8da0ef1-5579-5399-8df3-cc765d4308b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194238} {:answer/id #uuid "064f803f-57fc-5b41-84b4-fa08e0096e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194239} {:answer/id #uuid "43512849-4db1-5c38-8263-249522cd6afa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194240} {:answer/id #uuid "5d3cbb8d-f422-5ee5-8496-5ea357cb898a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194241} {:answer/id #uuid "6c90883d-5cf1-52f1-9ad4-ea88bf615d4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "064f803f-57fc-5b41-84b4-fa08e0096e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194239} :answer-field/id #uuid "95cc52ea-8c0b-5948-b0d1-2f9b00923bd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f4e361d-2d38-571b-8fc9-56865896c6d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-162919" :question/problem "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le x,\\,0\\le x\\le 1}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=3xy.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=3xy.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 3xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot {[{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33240905-4701-5489-bad5-983396955edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362903} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee50fad-1b9c-54a8-a718-d346dd6f26a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362904} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f964cd-6b10-54ed-a99b-55fab9170c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362905} {:answer/id #uuid "54f2e7bc-651e-5ee6-9c79-8bc293ed4e7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362906} {:answer/id #uuid "00c3bb50-dfa3-5735-9b29-b530faf81991" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3f964cd-6b10-54ed-a99b-55fab9170c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362905} :answer-field/id #uuid "436898f8-dee1-536c-9ced-18fc1b017ff2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51f31efc-ef25-5078-b42e-7e203fa42644" :question/math-academy-id "q-162974" :question/problem "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}15{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot (1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}-15{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[5{x}^{3}-3{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362908 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20936872-cdc9-5591-971d-5ab262ba9b00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362910} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd80545-6788-5ad3-b0b8-22d02c729458" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362911} {:answer/id #uuid "669280de-ebd8-562b-b86c-3e7e0fdf05e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362912} {:answer/id #uuid "9e062b6c-5651-537e-b1aa-65d477891b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362913} {:answer/id #uuid "e12407bf-c792-5554-bef3-bb3758950025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e062b6c-5651-537e-b1aa-65d477891b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362913} :answer-field/id #uuid "77731024-a26d-564c-b634-219e39134c97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2ec72a2-bd84-5cac-b0f8-c87f50fac582" :question/math-academy-id "q-162977" :question/problem "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,1\\le x\\le {e}^{y}}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{xy}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{xy}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{y}}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{x=1}^{x={e}^{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(9-1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362915 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bb12457-9677-57eb-ba11-5461a063e08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362917} {:answer/id #uuid "7fd63419-2f01-5c76-9635-a051cf3558fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362918} {:answer/id #uuid "c12a2ad0-831c-52ed-9eed-61d0671b61db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362919} {:answer/id #uuid "2b246fcc-c0dd-5eed-abc6-fc0a4c9843b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362920} {:answer/id #uuid "a10bf3e2-8457-5c64-bb56-d4c67005d617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b246fcc-c0dd-5eed-abc6-fc0a4c9843b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362920} :answer-field/id #uuid "b336e878-9100-5460-add8-4af383c0416b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b4389be5-537b-5699-b760-014d4f425b90" :question/math-academy-id "q-162984" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{y}$ is enclosed between the curve $y=2-{x}^{2}$ and  the line $y=1$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/2d08bcbbcd7ec4d8c388d24728c3f3afdc7c954497f342e9ac2b459fad24e5d2.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{3}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2-{x}^{2}}3\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3[y]_{y=1}^{y=2-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3[2-{x}^{2}-1]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3-3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[3x-{x}^{3}]}_{x=-1}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(3-1)-(-3+1) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362922 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50846b70-2834-5650-9048-35c41ff00991" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362924} {:answer/id #uuid "114d718d-b5bb-5a50-86d9-c228877d6192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362925} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f0863a-fe00-50d4-ae6d-6c94faa5f24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362926} {:answer/id #uuid "92b662ee-39a0-53dd-817e-3b652bfda00b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362927} {:answer/id #uuid "517d3f0f-1fd9-59c8-b054-7267aa97f0fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92b662ee-39a0-53dd-817e-3b652bfda00b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362927} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a03178a-4268-539b-aa8a-a11837c1e21f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362923}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "211db4ed-b9dc-5250-b1cf-47ab80a7c425" :question/math-academy-id "q-163053" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=15{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}$ is enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{2}$ and the line $y=1$ for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/28a3f0e1eda23169a649276a9cde34d3d96cdd75d5b2bc71c3535604612526e5.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=15{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 15{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}15{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}15{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}{y}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{2}{5}{y}^{5/2}]}_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}(1-|x{|}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}-6{x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{8}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(2-\\frac{3}{4})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fd94df3-8fa8-5a88-a171-bab7bad09cb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362931} {:answer/id #uuid "f25aa412-5cb4-5941-a466-3265c8051cca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362932} {:answer/id #uuid "ea8e9aa4-3a86-58e5-806a-2e362fdd840d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362933} {:answer/id #uuid "76a431c9-2e15-56de-896d-da0bfbce2189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362934} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbf7f1d-f64e-5c89-bc4f-578685bfef8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76a431c9-2e15-56de-896d-da0bfbce2189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362934} :answer-field/id #uuid "88bfc1a7-3f48-56b5-88ba-63568ea12888" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04a3a450-2480-5985-9ffe-c5a99c4b0b77" :question/math-academy-id "q-163062" :question/problem "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\le y\\le 0}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2{e}^{y}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=2{e}^{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 2{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{0}2x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{0}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{y=0}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x-2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=1/2}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{2}{3})-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1110a5b7-850e-53ea-b900-dece9029130d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362938} {:answer/id #uuid "9c3ca8e3-7cac-5748-9af6-d13bb06171dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362939} {:answer/id #uuid "a0322883-e49b-5298-9a1e-f29204a9f4b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362940} {:answer/id #uuid "c044b365-973d-5b7d-a554-6e06b9a48b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362941} {:answer/id #uuid "1007df5d-422e-5ae5-b75d-6154d8caac75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c3ca8e3-7cac-5748-9af6-d13bb06171dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362939} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ad5553a-f080-5472-928d-86f9eec29986" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4033870e-3887-5014-89df-65a433c79034" :question/math-academy-id "q-163066" :question/problem "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=5xy.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=5xy.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 5xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}5{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3y}5{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y{\\int }_{0}^{3y}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=3y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y(9{y}^{3}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}45{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[9{y}^{5}]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362943 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88c70b00-0281-5f87-b41d-d2b36af0df34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362945} {:answer/id #uuid "6f221915-102f-52ef-bd4f-31280a2378ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362946} {:answer/id #uuid "33ca6195-3391-504d-840b-b9df8e49c56a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362947} {:answer/id #uuid "dfb1b630-a0ea-57c4-8919-eb3dfd9597f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362948} {:answer/id #uuid "252c8705-bff5-5d00-a1f8-8309aa302e74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfb1b630-a0ea-57c4-8919-eb3dfd9597f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362948} :answer-field/id #uuid "4814b913-3172-5e09-a05c-159e5417c60c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7b1c9132-4ec9-56d7-922a-aa6d4bf001f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-163152" :question/problem "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le 1}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[x]_{x={y}^{2}}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}1-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=1/2}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{1}{3})-(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{24}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffa776c3-741e-52e0-b9b4-795910f03aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362952} {:answer/id #uuid "91e8e9f2-2496-593a-b242-ba70fbfec18a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362953} {:answer/id #uuid "368e461d-fddd-548d-b5a8-9895249f2f78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362954} {:answer/id #uuid "0ad98d09-b9ef-5411-b2c2-4ad5c1e02a84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362955} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f26564-7952-57be-abbe-e0d688fc8142" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ad98d09-b9ef-5411-b2c2-4ad5c1e02a84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362955} :answer-field/id #uuid "717be8fa-2ce4-5d63-a11c-4ed63830ec25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "799d0cdb-9a61-5e33-944e-eb81748dac59" :question/math-academy-id "q-163154" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x$ is enclosed between the line $y=4x$ and the $x$-axis for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/07701125c6acc36d127556bf95940bf0f74ba9ef3072f3af22dac26edc053a74.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 4x}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=x.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4x}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{y=0}^{y=4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1394733e-b18b-5759-90c3-a87afe348b55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362959} {:answer/id #uuid "57e8d47e-b539-564a-a9b1-c543480c1661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362960} {:answer/id #uuid "547cb537-a74e-5423-a1eb-7ddc8cd52abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362961} {:answer/id #uuid "a210b849-0b42-51e7-b227-24416b7ad9d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362962} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f44364-49e4-5be4-9ef8-2f70fbfa0b27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1f44364-49e4-5be4-9ef8-2f70fbfa0b27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362963} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e4d7a73-4760-5532-9c83-7513aad5616c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90b358c4-37e7-50a4-97fd-95d01efd5161" :question/math-academy-id "q-163155" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2y$ is enclosed between the line $y=\\sqrt{x}$ and the $x$-axis for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/ddc11fc93f034c3d650854e21f178716c941c18f12eb94123e1af2c835c47981.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=2y.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 2y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}2xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}2y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1469d538-e53e-5b3c-acd0-d0455ee7e0f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362966} {:answer/id #uuid "6426b621-0d7d-5eb7-b00b-0811b8418747" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362967} {:answer/id #uuid "8b027d77-9abc-503b-9edb-d3f55e6a4619" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362968} {:answer/id #uuid "8f77452d-bcd7-59c8-9215-46f297b26fa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362969} {:answer/id #uuid "0722bafd-e61b-5ed8-9635-1c4d92c23f93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6426b621-0d7d-5eb7-b00b-0811b8418747" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362967} :answer-field/id #uuid "148c3c7d-6b33-5c7f-af4d-1eb6722ca0d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f651953-b627-59da-a03c-bc3501f0957b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163166" :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{e}^{-y}\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3}$ and has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{xy}.$ Given that the mass of the lamina is $2$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{{e}^{-y}}^{1}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{x={e}^{-y}}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}0-(-y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d418d0a4-c635-5fb3-82b2-725ec21e4149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362973} {:answer/id #uuid "62260333-4d07-5577-8af5-954bade7532f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362974} {:answer/id #uuid "6c8e20a8-7f64-5c34-80d3-e9a90d2e4c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362975} {:answer/id #uuid "0332b99f-b11d-5969-a2d0-2f5dae65e286" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362976} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6d5ead-9fe7-51aa-ac9c-7f1ec2271e19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c8e20a8-7f64-5c34-80d3-e9a90d2e4c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362975} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ceb42f7-0c98-5500-8b1d-df0e02ace7ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6536c486-21ee-5d79-a4c6-aa5c7c74e471" :question/math-academy-id "q-163281" :question/problem "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}$ and is enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{3}$ and the $x$-axis for $1\\le x\\le 2.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $2$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/b6e8af58b8e7ba5f909d226b895bb39b3fc94e53686e4718eb32c9bb4ee61c08.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.$ \n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot [y]_{y=0}^{y={x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =4-1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ec69487-9385-55af-ae17-27029770f4b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362980} {:answer/id #uuid "31420013-9dac-5cfe-9d04-5679c8eac38c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362981} {:answer/id #uuid "e75a7462-cbc2-5c43-bf88-24805d6d15d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362982} {:answer/id #uuid "268a58e9-68ef-50b8-bea7-4f2c6fd9b5ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362983} {:answer/id #uuid "9f25bd4a-e20a-5611-ba97-dc5e3dce9c83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ec69487-9385-55af-ae17-27029770f4b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362980} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dd2c7f9-6e71-53f2-b63e-4b30ffaf127a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5123abff-afdd-5163-80ce-cbbc07bf474a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163282" :question/problem "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x+y$ and is enclosed between the curve $x=2y$ and the $y$-axis for $0\\le y\\le 1.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $\\frac{4}{3}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/3097e540292efd601743ba8de24acffc3b51469e77561b2bccbd799d1125e1ed.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=x+y.$ \n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot (x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}+xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}{x}^{2}+xy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8{y}^{3}}{3}+2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{14{y}^{3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{7{y}^{4}}{6}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{7}{6})}{(\\frac{4}{3})}=\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78c8650e-358c-5de3-ad27-6f82822dc816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362987} {:answer/id #uuid "d77d5f92-a33b-5b67-87f4-2155a625bea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362988} {:answer/id #uuid "9c035341-4a75-575b-9db0-97ebe638a89d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362989} {:answer/id #uuid "a8629456-085b-5056-b0f3-abab4b2ee818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362990} {:answer/id #uuid "6f75b3e0-d76a-5c76-98a4-d402aa25828c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78c8650e-358c-5de3-ad27-6f82822dc816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362987} :answer-field/id #uuid "71bce30e-5754-5b60-8bac-afac082c6733" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33a3b781-6acf-5dd0-b7cf-d6ee01942bff" :question/math-academy-id "q-163284" :question/problem "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}$ and the $x$-axis for $-2\\le y\\le 0.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\pi ,$ find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/14c292e8a224b59c143d0e8a57d43b554ce298cd4f44fc2169f516d683e8c35a.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}},\\,-2\\le y\\le 0}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\pi .$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{4-{y}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}4-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{[4y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }[0-(-8+\\frac{8}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ade97b3-3ae1-52f0-a660-f45c4eed2137" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362994} {:answer/id #uuid "2306a1c0-5717-58af-af3e-31d99274ea46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362995} {:answer/id #uuid "9d349b4b-bbba-5f3b-9089-6ed2a4ec9289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362996} {:answer/id #uuid "8b074062-4e25-5d62-8d85-ee909d4980dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362997} {:answer/id #uuid "6686e8a9-2553-5213-845c-56f964adc1c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d349b4b-bbba-5f3b-9089-6ed2a4ec9289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362996} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee81b702-4f56-543d-ab2a-e611150faabd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50932592-cdce-5657-b95b-4cf478865951" :question/math-academy-id "q-163289" :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y},\\,0\\le y\\le 4}.$ Given that the area of the lamina is $\\frac{16}{3}$ square units, find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c25cfb01-3c2f-5d34-bc06-726402b0c3b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363001} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a2eec6-0c4e-5809-bc7d-cd04c9d73333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363002} {:answer/id #uuid "5e4e375a-2393-5013-a61d-0a76ccc003ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363003} {:answer/id #uuid "f927540e-d2b4-59f9-8404-3af5a98e8b0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363004} {:answer/id #uuid "71c2eeff-c271-58cc-9a39-e3c09e69e68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c25cfb01-3c2f-5d34-bc06-726402b0c3b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363001} :answer-field/id #uuid "c05ae583-b19b-558d-8a24-5873d2d8897f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76a92f29-dc89-5d7c-8114-3440057bc759" :question/math-academy-id "q-163503" :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}.$ Given that the area of the lamina is $\\pi $ square units, find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{[4x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }(8-\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "198dbaa0-6aae-5562-839e-c47b2c007959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363008} {:answer/id #uuid "c3233fac-f41a-5e7c-9a70-cf7cdbebae7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363009} {:answer/id #uuid "ab0e9c64-0944-5a28-9334-0f8fd3ca98ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363010} {:answer/id #uuid "85764bc8-9962-5e7e-a5ab-02cd0f23a0f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363011} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5f2230-525c-541a-811f-7f053d4392ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab0e9c64-0944-5a28-9334-0f8fd3ca98ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363010} :answer-field/id #uuid "74b0e5b4-82ac-55ea-922e-a06b356ae442" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9b3e654-4269-55a4-b9b1-db4c550125a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-163504" :question/problem "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x={y}^{2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-2\\le y\\le 0.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\frac{8}{3},$ find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/a8c57b12334a23542bae73ba1ac6848e69830b9663a1f83b6340f6812974f416.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2},\\,-2\\le y\\le 0}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\frac{8}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}y\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y[x]_{x=0}^{x={y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y({y}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot (0-4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b0cc919-a7f4-5469-bb19-b4df8bb0b346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{44}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197570} {:answer/id #uuid "d22de37c-9302-5d49-af08-9fb7eb6e0ff7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{155}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197571} {:answer/id #uuid "dc3738b1-84ae-5158-b581-e99f3f163d93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{85}{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197572} {:answer/id #uuid "0f3c3d9b-adce-54c7-88e9-b44b1cde564c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{91}{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197573} {:answer/id #uuid "55a68612-fb29-59e4-86f2-5bbd2f9681f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{75}{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc3738b1-84ae-5158-b581-e99f3f163d93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{85}{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197572} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bdb8f1e-2955-5b64-b3bf-298c1cb51ca5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c002c85-6997-51d7-b78d-ab1c68bac4cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-39020" :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}$ and has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=4xy.$ Given that the mass of the lamina is $21$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 4xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}4x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4x{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4x{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y={x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{8}}{6}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{256}{6}-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{85}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{85}{2})}{21}=\\frac{85}{42}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eee28a03-bb27-5562-ba3b-adf60082f952" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197642} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7f47f3-0def-5291-b68e-2dc459bac22c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197643} {:answer/id #uuid "465e9201-5d3d-5974-85a2-bf8bc6b3c80f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197644} {:answer/id #uuid "5db2a774-be1c-55ad-9062-0e5e361bb1e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197645} {:answer/id #uuid "74959f29-b227-57b5-af43-862535f5982d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef7f47f3-0def-5291-b68e-2dc459bac22c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197643} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe8f78ac-0006-5eca-af2d-26d93a114de6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197641}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f0a3ecd-2e89-53d3-99a9-57716fabd869" :question/math-academy-id "q-39540" :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-x\\le y\\le x}.$ Given that the area of the lamina is $4$ square units, find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x{\\int }_{-x}^{x}\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x[y]_{y=-x}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80d9395c-82a1-5efe-9469-cb2bcfe66bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197648} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ab7110-d1f1-5c79-bcbe-a6224a167b29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197649} {:answer/id #uuid "19760eaa-4b5d-5bb9-a32f-0886a8d4460f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197650} {:answer/id #uuid "43900f67-a26c-55f9-832c-e815f5ec6b2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197651} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca432fb-1f91-5b9a-af72-3a74eef9ac2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80d9395c-82a1-5efe-9469-cb2bcfe66bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197648} :answer-field/id #uuid "2757a6b5-87d8-51f1-b9a0-4e1f636095d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197647}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38ead2a6-fa96-5840-9429-dd70fd1bb582" :question/math-academy-id "q-39547" :question/problem "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)={y}^{2}$ and is enclosed between the curve $x=1-{y}^{2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $\\frac{4}{15}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/78f9da3d48727d2cb3c447be0f4050a044c4aabe29179fd31f04cd7b6c66eabd.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1-{y}^{2},\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)={y}^{2}.$ \n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot (1-2{y}^{2}+{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{2}-2{y}^{4}+{y}^{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}-2{y}^{4}+{y}^{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{2}{5}{y}^{5}+\\frac{1}{7}{y}^{7}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{105}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{8}{105})}{(\\frac{4}{15})}=\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$"}]}
